{"type":"message","id":"3be9b613","parentId":"481d35ca","timestamp":"2026-03-16T10:04:12.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Q6bSz484qflafBALY8lniivP|fc_0a43ffedc4cd476a0169b7d59044b08191a111fc453c8ebd95","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-cancer-detector/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: kidney-cancer-detection\ndescription: Use this skill when the user wants to analyze a kidney medical image for possible kidney cancer detection, classify the result, or route a kidney image through the upload API and then into the kidney cancer prediction endpoint using the returned remote image path.\n---\n\n# Kidney Cancer Detection\n\nUpload the local image first, then run inference with the uploaded remote path.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Determine the local image to analyze.\n   - Prefer an explicit local file path when one is available.\n   - If no path is provided, use the most recent supported image under `./config/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON and build the new remote `image_path` by concatenating:\n   - `path + filename`\n5. Call the kidney cancer inference endpoint using that uploaded `image_path`.\n\n## Fixed request values\n\nKeep these values static:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- inference endpoint `data.storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n\n## What this skill runs\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script automatically selects the newest supported image from `./config/media/inbound`.\n\n## Upload response handling\n\nGiven an upload response like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"path\": \"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/\",\n  \"filename\": \"9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\",\n  \"column_names\": null\n}\n```\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nimage_path = \"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\"\n```\n\nUse that full value as the inference request's `data.image_path`.\n\n## Expected output\n\nReturn validated JSON with this shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"uploaded_image_path\": \"string\",\n  \"prediction_label\": \"string\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.98\n}\n```\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/kidney-cancer-detector/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: kidney-cancer-detection\\ndescription: Use this skill when the user wants to analyze a kidney medical image for possible kidney cancer detection, classify the result, or route a kidney image through the upload API and then into the kidney cancer prediction endpoint using the returned remote image path.\\n---\\n\\n# Kidney Cancer Detection\\n\\nUpload the local image first, then run inference with the uploaded remote path.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Determine the local image to analyze.\\n   - Prefer an explicit local file path when one is available.\\n   - If no path is provided, use the most recent supported image under `./config/media/inbound`.\\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\\n4. Read the upload response JSON and build the new remote `image_path` by concatenating:\\n   - `path + filename`\\n5. Call the kidney cancer inference endpoint using that uploaded `image_path`.\\n\\n## Fixed request values\\n\\nKeep these values static:\\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\\n- inference endpoint `data.storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n\\n## What this skill runs\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\\n```\\n\\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script automatically selects the newest supported image from `./config/media/inbound`.\\n\\n## Upload response handling\\n\\nGiven an upload response like:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/\\\",\\n  \\\"filename\\\": \\\"9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"column_names\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBuild:\\n\\n```text\\nimage_path = \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\"\\n```\\n\\nUse that full value as the inference request's `data.image_path`.\\n\\n## Expected output\\n\\nReturn validated JSON with this shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"uploaded_image_path\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"prediction_label\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.98\\n}\\n```\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":155,"output":687,"cacheRead":17280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18122,"cost":{"input":0.00038750000000000004,"output":0.010305,"cacheRead":0.00432,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015012500000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773655439138}}
