 a new repository here? No, that doesn’t seem right either. I just want to finalize this in a concise way, but the situation is a bit tangled, and I need to sort it out.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Done.\n\nWhat I changed:\n- Removed the static image-path behavior from `~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-cancer-detector/scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py`.\n- Added an upload step that:\n  - sends the local image as `POST multipart/form-data`\n  - keeps `storage_ref=nodes_bucket` and `local_file_path=upload/` fixed\n  - replaces `user_id` with the provided Telegram user ID\n- Reads the upload response and builds the new inference `image_path` as `path + filename`.\n- Uses that uploaded `image_path` for the kidney cancer detection request.\n- Updated `SKILL.md` to document the new workflow and usage.\n\nNew usage:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nNotes:\n- If `local-image-path` is omitted, the script now tries to use the newest supported image from `./config/media/inbound`.\n- I also cleaned up the skill frontmatter so it matches the expected skill format.\n- I validated the script locally with `py_compile` and `--help`.\n\nOne caveat:\n- I could not create a git commit because `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace` is not a git repository in this environment.\n\nIf you want, I can also make the script automatically pull the Telegram user ID from message/session metadata instead of requiring `--telegram-user-id`/`TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0a43ffedc4cd476a0169b7d5afc6788191816a512b3d4309cb\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":135,"output":345,"cacheRead":18560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19040,"cost":{"input":0.0003375,"output":0.005175,"cacheRead":0.00464,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0101525}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773655462009}}
